              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اقامتگاه (eqâmatgâh) — \"lodgings, a place to stay; a residence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اقامتگاه (eqâmatgâh) ما نزدیک دریا بود. Eqâmatgâh-e mâ nazdik-e daryâ bud. Our lodgings were near the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Eqâmatgâh-e bumgardi — a guesthouse in a village home, now common in the countryside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "eqâmatgâh is built from eqâmat 'a stay', a loan usually traced to Arabic iqāma 'staying, residing', and native gâh 'place'. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
